%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: Flowing Type — a specimen sheet for artkit's paragraph layout
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 600 600
%%EndComments

% Specimen sheet for artkit's paragraph/flowing-text section (issue
% #16, lib/artkit.ps): four quadrants, one capability each. Top-left is
% tfblock left-aligned in a plain box; top-right is the same box under
% /justify, showing every non-last line stretched flush to both
% margins while the paragraph's true last line falls back to /left;
% bottom-left is tfcols carrying one run of copy across two columns,
% the second column picking up exactly where the first's leftover
% stopped; bottom-right calls tfflow directly with a custom boundsproc
% -- available width computed from a circle's own equation -- to flow
% text into a round medallion instead of a rectangle, the "arbitrary
% region" capability tfblock/tfcols are just convenience wrappers over.
% Run from the repo root:
%
%   pscat --page 600x600 examples/paragraph_layout.ps

(lib/artkit.ps) run

1 1 1 setrgbcolor clippath fill

/Palatino-Bold findfont 22 scalefont setfont
0.1 0.1 0.12 setrgbcolor
(Flowing Type) 300 566 showctr
/Palatino-Italic findfont 12 scalefont setfont
(tfblock left + justify, tfcols, tfflow with a custom region) 300 548 showctr

/COPY (Artkit now flows a paragraph the way alongpath flows a brush: word by word, measured by its own width, breaking where the line runs out of room and starting fresh on the next.) def

% --- top-left: tfblock, /left -------------------------------------------
0.1 0.1 0.12 setrgbcolor
/Palatino findfont 11 scalefont setfont
newpath 30 300 250 220 rectstroke
30 300 250 220 15 /left COPY tfblock pop

% --- top-right: tfblock, /justify ----------------------------------------
newpath 320 300 250 220 rectstroke
320 300 250 220 15 /justify COPY tfblock pop

% --- bottom-left: tfcols, two columns sharing one run of copy ------------
/LONGCOPY (Wrapping, justification, margins and leading, columns, and an arbitrary region are the five things this section adds: pick a box or write your own boundsproc, and the words find their own way to the edge.) def
newpath 30 30 120 220 rectstroke
newpath 160 30 120 220 rectstroke
30 30 120 10 220 2 14 /left LONGCOPY tfcols pop

% --- bottom-right: tfflow, a circular medallion --------------------------
/MEDX 450 def /MEDY 140 def /MEDR 95 def
newpath MEDX MEDY MEDR 0 360 arc stroke
{
    /medy exch def
    /meddy medy MEDY sub def
    meddy dup mul MEDR MEDR mul ge
        { MEDX MEDX }
        { /medhw MEDR MEDR mul meddy meddy mul sub sqrt 6 sub dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if def
          MEDX medhw sub MEDX medhw add }
    ifelse
} MEDY MEDR add 10 sub MEDY MEDR sub 10 add 14 /center
(Set within a circle, not a box -- the region a caller's own boundsproc describes.)
tfflow pop

showpage
